    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Readme'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/DataQualityDashboard/192582?rev=' id='Readme' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/DataQualityDashboard' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='600' maxwidth='1400' minheight='600' minwidth='1400' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97334' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='1333'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Glossary</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The purpose behind Data Quality dashboard is to report the health status of the entire data in Data Hub through some select metrics that best reflect the current data quality in Data Hub. This data is produced by running regular tests on the tables and conveying the results through the data quality dimensions and global quality monitoring.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Data Quality Dimensions</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>In Data Hub, DDUs can set up Great Expectations (GE) tests to run on their data. All of the different expectation types are mapped to a “metric type” by DataHub based on the definitions in this document. The exact mapping per expectation                                                      </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>We use the following Data Quality Dimensions to evaluate data quality and these are mapped to “metric type” in GE.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Completeness: Completeness is measured as the percentage of data records in the table compared to the expectation (upstream table / data source). </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Correctness: Correctness is measured as the percentage of data records with values that match a known source of truth, or are within expected thresholds.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Uniqueness: Uniqueness is measured as the percentage of data records where all primary key values are unique.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Validity: Validity is measured as the percentage of data records where all values are in the required format. Data should be of the correct type and align with any formatting rules.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>You can find further information on Data quality dimensions</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Global Quality Monitoring </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Some data quality checks will be automatically run by DataHub if your datasets have some basic features. Details of these default checks can be found here: </run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='7333' id='5' name='Sheet 25' show-title='false' w='15286' x='6214' y='47167' />
        <zone h='5000' id='6' name='Sheet 26' show-title='false' w='24929' x='68429' y='82667' />
        <zone h='4500' id='7' name='Sheet 27' show-title='false' w='4571' x='27143' y='69000' />
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='31' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='97334' id='30' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98858' x='571' y='1333'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='97334' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='1333'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Glossary</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The purpose behind Data Quality dashboard is to report the health status of the entire data in Data Hub through some select metrics that best reflect the current data quality in Data Hub. This data is produced by running regular tests on the tables and conveying the results through the data quality dimensions and global quality monitoring.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Data Quality Dimensions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>In Data Hub, DDUs can set up Great Expectations (GE) tests to run on their data. All of the different expectation types are mapped to a “metric type” by DataHub based on the definitions in this document. The exact mapping per expectation                                                      </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>We use the following Data Quality Dimensions to evaluate data quality and these are mapped to “metric type” in GE.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Completeness: Completeness is measured as the percentage of data records in the table compared to the expectation (upstream table / data source). </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Correctness: Correctness is measured as the percentage of data records with values that match a known source of truth, or are within expected thresholds.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Uniqueness: Uniqueness is measured as the percentage of data records where all primary key values are unique.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Validity: Validity is measured as the percentage of data records where all values are in the required format. Data should be of the correct type and align with any formatting rules.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>You can find further information on Data quality dimensions</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='24'>Global Quality Monitoring </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Some data quality checks will be automatically run by DataHub if your datasets have some basic features. Details of these default checks can be found here: </run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='44' h='7333' id='5' is-fixed='true' name='Sheet 25' show-title='false' w='15286' x='6214' y='47167'>
